WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.056 --> 00:00:14.001
"You say that I've been kind to you?"

2
00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:18.143
The earl repeated his question to Cedric in the castle library.

3
00:00:18.163 --> 00:00:22.725
Dougal, the earl's dog, sat next to Cedric's chair.

4
00:00:22.745 --> 00:00:24.845
"Oh, yes!

5
00:00:25.346 --> 00:00:29.687
I'm forever grateful to you for helping the apple seller and Dick and Mary."

6
00:00:31.744 --> 00:00:33.265
"The apple seller!"

7
00:00:33.685 --> 00:00:34.866
the earl exclaimed.

8
00:00:34.886 --> 00:00:37.307
"Dick! Mary!

9
00:00:37.327 --> 00:00:39.308
Who are these people?"

10
00:00:39.328 --> 00:00:42.830
"I forgot that you've never met them!"

11
00:00:44.731 --> 00:00:45.672
Cedric laughed.

12
00:00:46.452 --> 00:00:48.093
"They're special friends of mine.

13
00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:51.415
I helped them with the money that you gave to Mr.

14
00:00:51.455 --> 00:00:55.217
Havisham. You said I could spend it any way I liked."

15
00:00:57.138 --> 00:00:59.620
Cedric explained what he'd done for his friends.

16
00:01:01.472 --> 00:01:05.174
While Cedric talked, the earl quietly observed the dog.

17
00:01:09.395 --> 00:01:13.297
usually doesn't make friends quickly," the earl thought.

18
00:01:13.317 --> 00:01:17.099
"But he liked this young fellow right away."

19
00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.901
At that moment the big dog put his head on the boy's knee.

20
00:01:23.281 --> 00:01:25.502
Cedric petted him while continuing to talk.

21
00:01:26.763 --> 00:01:29.004
"You'd like Dick," Cedric said.

22
00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.221
"He does everything fair and square."

23
00:01:32.241 --> 00:01:35.482
"What on earth does that mean?"

24
00:01:35.502 --> 00:01:43.204
"Well Cedric wasn't quite sure, but he knew it was something positive.

25
00:01:43.224 --> 00:01:49.325
"I think it means he wouldn't cheat anyone," Cedric said slowly.

26
00:01:50.726 --> 00:01:53.627
He sat forward in his chair as he grew more confident.

27
00:01:53.647 --> 00:01:55.407
"That's right.

28
00:01:56.007 --> 00:01:58.468
Or hit a boy who was smaller than he was.

29
00:01:59.636 --> 00:02:01.958
He's really dedicated to his work too.

30
00:02:03.199 --> 00:02:06.621
He makes sure his customers' shoes are as shiny as possible."

31
00:02:08.663 --> 00:02:11.805
Cedric reached into his pocket and pulled out Dick's handkerchief.

32
00:02:13.286 --> 00:02:17.669
He regarded it with a mix of affection and pride before handing it to the earl.

33
00:02:17.689 --> 00:02:23.473
"Dick gave me a present before the ship sailed."

34
00:02:23.493 --> 00:02:27.156
"Um it's very bright."

35
00:02:28.652 --> 00:02:30.953
The earl quickly handed back the handkerchief.

36
00:02:30.973 --> 00:02:33.715
"I'm going to keep it forever."

37
00:02:35.636 --> 00:02:39.238
Cedric admired the handkerchief again before returning it to his pocket.

38
00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:44.621
"And this Dick is one of your acquaintances, is he?"

39
00:02:45.142 --> 00:02:46.242
the earl asked.

40
00:02:46.262 --> 00:02:48.924
"He's an old friend.

41
00:02:49.945 --> 00:02:52.126
Well, not quite as old as Mr.

42
00:02:52.146 --> 00:02:53.787
Hobbs," Cedric said.

43
00:02:53.807 --> 00:02:57.469
"Oh! I haven't told you about Mr.

44
00:02:57.509 --> 00:02:59.911
Hobbs the grocer—my best friend."

45
00:03:01.373 --> 00:03:04.355
The earl couldn't imagine what Cedric would say next.

46
00:03:05.676 --> 00:03:11.761
He was still trying to grasp that his grandson's friends were a shoeshine boy, an apple seller, and

47
00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:12.441
a servant.

48
00:03:14.103 --> 00:03:16.285
Cedric continued talking about the grocer.

49
00:03:16.305 --> 00:03:17.906
"I bought Mr.

50
00:03:17.926 --> 00:03:19.127
Hobbs a gold watch.

51
00:03:20.008 --> 00:03:21.649
That's something else I did with your money.

52
00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:28.329
I had it inscribed with some poetry: When this you see, remember me."

53
00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:33.030
Cedric sighed.

54
00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:35.751
"I'll always remember Mr.

55
00:03:35.791 --> 00:03:38.372
Hobbs—and my other friends too."

56
00:03:40.612 --> 00:03:43.393
In his travels, the earl had seen a great deal of the world.

57
00:03:44.653 --> 00:03:49.675
But here in his own home was something so unusual that it took his breath away.

58
00:03:50.835 --> 00:03:53.796
The earl had never liked children, not even his own.

59
00:03:55.308 --> 00:04:00.492
But this boy—this American boy—was actually entertaining.

60
00:04:02.233 --> 00:04:05.855
The door to the library opened, and a footman entered.

61
00:04:05.875 --> 00:04:09.618
"Dinner is served, my lord," he said.

62
00:04:11.299 --> 00:04:14.161
Cedric stood up and studied the earl's gouty foot.

63
00:04:14.181 --> 00:04:18.444
"Would you like me to help you?"

64
00:04:18.864 --> 00:04:19.504
Cedric said.

65
00:04:19.524 --> 00:04:22.627
"You could lean on me when you walk.

66
00:04:24.007 --> 00:04:26.849
One time a potato barrel rolled over Mr.

67
00:04:26.889 --> 00:04:27.709
Hobbs' foot.

68
00:04:28.849 --> 00:04:31.910
Afterward his foot hurt, so he leaned on me."

69
00:04:33.891 --> 00:04:36.271
The earl looked his grandson up and down.

70
00:04:36.291 --> 00:04:40.172
"Are you sure you could support me?"

71
00:04:40.192 --> 00:04:44.374
"I think I could," Cedric said.

72
00:04:44.394 --> 00:04:48.795
"I'm pretty strong, and you could use your cane on the other side.

73
00:04:49.955 --> 00:04:52.976
Dick said I have a lot of muscle for a nine-year-old."

74
00:04:53.972 --> 00:04:57.315
Cedric held up both arms and flexed his muscles for the earl.

75
00:04:57.335 --> 00:05:04.381
"All right, you may try," his grandfather replied.

76
00:05:06.062 --> 00:05:08.945
Cedric handed the earl his cane and helped him to stand.

77
00:05:10.346 --> 00:05:12.187
Usually this was the footman's job.

78
00:05:14.389 --> 00:05:18.713
If the earl felt any pain in his foot, he relieved it by shouting at the footman.

79
00:05:20.774 --> 00:05:24.113
But this time he didn't shout—even when his foot hurt.

80
00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:29.738
"Don't be afraid to lean on my shoulder," Cedric said with an encouraging smile.

81
00:05:29.758 --> 00:05:31.940
"I'll walk slowly."

82
00:05:33.602 --> 00:05:36.304
The earl didn't hesitate to rest his weight on Cedric.

83
00:05:37.586 --> 00:05:40.208
He wanted to see how much strength the boy possessed.

84
00:05:43.051 --> 00:05:46.053
When they entered the dining room, Cedric's heart sank.

85
00:05:47.335 --> 00:05:48.576
He was already tired.

86
00:05:50.324 --> 00:05:53.186
It was a long way to the earl's chair at the head of the table.

87
00:05:56.368 --> 00:06:01.472
By the time he'd helped the earl to sit, Cedric's face was red and he was panting.

88
00:06:01.492 --> 00:06:06.775
"Perhaps the heat from the fireplace helps your foot."

89
00:06:08.756 --> 00:06:10.998
Cedric wiped his forehead with Dick's handkerchief.

90
00:06:11.018 --> 00:06:14.340
"But it seems a bit warm to me."

91
00:06:16.161 --> 00:06:19.904
The earl noted Cedric's courage and his respectful attitude.

92
00:06:21.396 --> 00:06:25.202
"You've been doing some hard work," the earl said.

93
00:06:26.905 --> 00:06:28.467
Cedric wiped his face again.

94
00:06:28.487 --> 00:06:33.535
"It wasn't too hard, but a person does get warm in the summer."
